# =============================================================================
#  STM32H7 Autonomy Demo — Renode Simulation Script
# =============================================================================
#
# Usage:
#   > renode drone_simulation.resc
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Renode v1.16+ (https://renode.io)
#   - Firmware ELF at ../.pio/build/nucleo_h753zi/firmware.elf
#     (build with: pio run -e nucleo_h753zi)
#
# Simulated peripherals (see stm32h753.repl / Renode's stock stm32h753.repl):
#   USART3  @ 0x40004800 -> telemetry output (TelemetryLink uses UartDriver
#                           instance 3, i.e. USART3 -- NOT UART4; the two
#                           are easy to confuse since RM0433 lists UART4
#                           right after USART3 in the memory map)
#   TIM2    @ 0x40000000 -> PWM motor outputs
#   I2C1    @ 0x40005400 -> MPU6050 IMU bus
#   ADC1    @ 0x40022000 -> battery voltage (peripheral name: adcM1S2)
#   GPIOA..K              -> LEDs, button, motor PWM AF
#
# Notes:
#  - Renode does not ship a stock MPU6050/IMU peripheral model, so I2C1 has
#    no simulated slave attached here. Firmware IMU reads will read back
#    zeros / NACK -- this only affects the (currently unused) autonomy IMU
#    path, not boot, arm/disarm, or telemetry.
#  - CommandReceiver::ingest() is not called anywhere in this firmware, on
#    any UART. There is currently no wiring from a UART RX interrupt (or any
#    other source) into the command receiver, so sending "arm"/"takeoff"/etc.
#    bytes to any UART in this simulation has no effect on the vehicle state
#    -- this is a gap in the firmware itself, not a simulation limitation.
# =============================================================================

using sysbus

mach create "stm32h753_drone"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @stm32h753.repl

# --- Load the firmware ELF ---
$elf ?= @../.pio/build/nucleo_h753zi/firmware.elf
sysbus LoadELF $elf

# --- USART3 (telemetry) analyzer ---
showAnalyzer usart3

# --- ADC1 battery / VREFINT samples ---
adcM1S2 SetDefaultValue 2500 0   # Channel 0: battery = 12.5 V (2.0 divider -> 2.5 V at pin)
adcM1S2 SetDefaultValue 1650 1   # Channel 1: VREFINT = 1.65 V

# --- Start simulation ---
start

# --- Print banner ---
log "============================================"
log "  STM32H7 AUTONOMY DEMO — RENODE SIMULATION"
log "============================================"
log "  USART3 telemetry:       connected"
log "  ADC1 battery:           @ 12.5 V"
log "  LED (PA5):              toggling at boot"
log "  Button (PC13):          pull-up, active low"
log "============================================"
log "  GPIOA ODR is at 0x58020014 -- 'sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x58020014'"
log "  lets you check LED state headlessly (bit 5)."
log "  NOTE: sending bytes to any UART does not arm/command the"
log "  vehicle -- CommandReceiver.ingest() is not wired to any RX path."
log "============================================"
